  "question": {
    "text": "In a triangle $\\mathrm{ABC}$, medians $\\mathrm{AD}$ and $\\mathrm{BE}$ are drawn. If $\\mathrm{AD}=4, \\angle \\mathrm{DAB}=\\frac{\\pi}{6}$ and $\\angle \\mathrm{ABE}=\\frac{\\pi}{3}$, then the area of the $\\triangle \\mathrm{ABC}$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{64}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{8}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$\\frac{16}{3}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\nNone of these",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"assets\\st0027_807984779052.png\"><br> $\\tan 60^{\\circ}=\\frac{8 / 3}{x}$ or $x=\\frac{8}{3 \\sqrt{3}}$<img src=\"assets\\st0027_0098991e9b29.png\"><br>Area of $\\triangle \\mathrm{ABD}=\\frac{1}{2} \\times 4 \\times \\frac{8}{3 \\sqrt{3}}=\\frac{16}{3 \\sqrt{3}}$"
  }
